##Summary

The factorial of a positive integer n is the product of all positive integers from 1 to n. It can be calculated using both iterative and recursive approaches.

In the iterative method, a loop is used to multiply the numbers from 1 to n. In the recursive method, the function calls itself with a smaller value until it reaches the base condition n = 0 or n = 1.

##conclusion

The implementation and time analysis show that both iterative and recursive methods can be effectively used to calculate the factorial of a number. Both methods have O(n) time complexity, but the iterative approach is more memory-efficient because it requires only O(1) extra space.
